# Byte-code caches. Tracked by accident before this file existed, and
# `git rm --cached` on them was part of adding it: a .pyc changes on
# every run, so it puts a line in every diff and buries the source
# change that was actually made.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The environment and the runner's own state. `uv` rebuilds the first
# from uv.lock; the second is the pytest run's, and neither is a fact
# about the project.
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# A corpus's own graph, when acciughe is run against this repository's
# notes. The store holds a copy of every note's text, so it must never be
# committed.
.acciughe/

# Stray stores and sessions from a state directory pointed here. The graph
# belongs in the branch now; what is left is a reader who has been running
# an older acciughe, or a --state of their own inside the tree.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.jsonl
